\f5\fs28 \cf2 This is a collection of essays on 
\f6\i Dream of the Red Chamber
\f5\i0 . With delicate and perceptive writing, the author guides readers in deciphering the hidden codes embedded within the original text. In the author\'92s interpretation, 
\f6\i Dream of the Red Chamber
\f5\i0  speaks of emotion, of sensibility, and of the art of navigating the world. Its ultimate destination is not emptiness; rather, love and beauty remain its enduring themes.\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\sl324\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
The design begins with the text itself, distilling its literary imagery into highly refined visual expressions. Before each chapter, layered graphic forms with a distinctly contemporary aesthetic are introduced, creating a highly recognizable visual language. These interventions are intended to leave space beyond the text, inviting readers\'92 imagination to unfold.\
\
The overall design is positioned as contemporary elegance. Its color palette draws inspiration from the hues used in the Qing-dynasty illustrations of 
\f6\i Dream of the Red Chamber
\f5\i0  by Sun Wen. Transitional pages between chapters extract patterns from the costumes of the figures and the architectural ornamentation depicted in the original illustrations. On this foundation, brightness and saturation are heightened, while cool grays are introduced to balance and harmonize contrast. The decorative motifs are carefully simplified and abstracted. Through this interplay of color and ornament, the design seeks to evoke the flourishing splendor of the Grand View Garden, allowing readers to immerse themselves in its poetic abundance.}